// ============================================================================
// CHRISTIAN RELIGIOUS EDUCATION GRADE 4: skills, prerequisites and the misconception library (authoring source).
// Written offline by Claude (13 Nov 2026), no model call. Everything here is DRAFT until a CRE teacher who knows the
// school's tradition reviews it (docs/qa/cre-g4-review-*.md lists what to check).
// scripts/build-cre-g4.mjs merges it into curriculum/cre/g4.json (HOREB owns that file; the KICD rubrics are never touched)
// and writes the in-app map. Keys: 'THE_LI.FORGIVENESS' = the sub-strand CRE.G4.THE_LI.FORGIVENESS.
//
// Rules this file follows (owner's brief): Bible references are the ones the KICD design itself gives, and every fact asked is
// stated in that passage; no denominational claims (no numbering of the Ten Commandments, no teaching on how baptism is done or
// how the Lord's Supper works, no count of books that differs between traditions); values, prayer, worship and personal faith are
// for teacher observation, never scored; Islamic and Hindu RE are not loaded.
// Skill codes start CRES (four capitals the registry needs); the official outcome codes stay CRE.G4.
// Misconception codes all start M_C4_ so that the joined maps of Grades 4 and 5 never clash.
// Outcome letters: where the design's text layer repeated a letter (a, b, c twice because two columns were read), a skill that
// names the letter covers every outcome that carries it; in SELF_AWARENESS and MY_FAMILY the repeats are three and two real
// groups of outcomes, so those skills name the exact code suffix ('a_', 'b__').
// ============================================================================
